  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    \n    for c in range(10):\n        rows = []\n        cols = []\n        for r in range(R):\n            for col in range(C):\n                if grid[r][col] == c:\n                    rows.append(r)\n                    cols.append(col)\n        \n        if not rows:\n            continue\n            \n        min_r, max_r = min(rows), max(rows)\n        min_c, max_c = min(cols), max(cols)\n        \n        if max_r - min_r > 1 and max_c - min_c > 1:\n            is_box = True\n            \n            # Check if border is fully `c`\n            for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n                if grid[r][min_c] != c or grid[r][max_c] != c:\n                    is_box = False\n                    break\n            for col in range(min_c, max_c + 1):\n                if grid[min_r][col] != c or grid[max_r][col] != c:\n                    is_box = False\n                    break\n                    \n            if is_box:\n                # Check if `c` appears inside the box\n                inside_c = False\n                for r in range(min_r + 1, max_r):\n                    for col in range(min_c + 1, max_c):\n                        if grid[r][col] == c:\n                            inside_c = True\n                            \n                # Check if `c` appears outside the box\n                # (Since min/max are derived from all `c`, it can't be outside, \n                # but it's guaranteed to be exactly the box if inside_c is False)\n                if not inside_c:\n                    out = []\n                    for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n                        out.append(grid[r][min_c:max_c+1])\n                    return out\n                    \n    return grid\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    \n    for c in range(10):\n        rows = []\n        cols = []\n        for r in range(R):\n            for col in range(C):\n                if grid[r][col] == c:\n                    rows.append(r)\n                    cols.append(col)\n        \n        if not rows:\n            continue\n            \n        min_r, max_r = min(rows), max(rows)\n        min_c, max_c = min(cols), max(cols)\n        \n        if max_r - min_r > 1 and max_c - min_c > 1:\n            is_box = True\n            \n            # Check if border is fully `c`\n            for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n                if grid[r][min_c] != c or grid[r][max_c] != c:\n                    is_box = False\n                    break\n            for col in range(min_c, max_c + 1):\n                if grid[min_r][col] != c or grid[max_r][col] != c:\n                    is_box = False\n                    break\n                    \n            if is_box:\n                # Check if `c` appears inside the box\n                inside_c = False\n                for r in range(min_r + 1, max_r):\n                    for col in range(min_c + 1, max_c):\n                        if grid[r][col] == c:\n                            inside_c = True\n                            \n                # Check if `c` appears outside the box\n                # (Since min/max are derived from all `c`, it can't be outside, \n                # but it's guaranteed to be exactly the box if inside_c is False)\n                if not inside_c:\n                    out = []\n                    for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n                        out.append(grid[r][min_c:max_c+1])\n                    return out\n                    \n    return grid",
